WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.057 --> 00:00:02.980
- "Saturday Night Live" has
so many New York moments

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.630
that it's been crazy for
me to even think about,

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.510
but probably one of my
biggest and most fond memories

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.633
was the SNL 40th Anniversary Party.

00:00:13.528 --> 00:00:14.720
The after parties are always fun,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.720
but this after party was
the 40th anniversary,

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.830
and everyone who was anyone,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.070
it was just crazy amount
of people were there.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:23.600
And as soon as I walked in,

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.280
Paul McCartney was calling
my name to go onstage.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.100
And he was there with Dan
Aykroyd and Jim Belushi.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.317
And I got on stage and Dan Aykroyd said,

00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:35.790
"Kid (claps) I've done this
for 40 years, it's your turn.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.390
You gotta rock this party."

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.110
And so there was no band, it was just me,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.580
and Paul McCartney, and Dan, we did one,

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.690
and we just had people
come up from the crowd

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.150
and play and jam out and play songs.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.600
And the end of the night,
we're on stage singing

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.400
with Bill Murray and
Chris Rock and Chappelle,

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.617
and Dave Chappelle goes to me,

00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:56.910
"Jimmy, if you ask
nicely, I think he's here,

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.610
but if you ask, you could
probably get Prince to come up."

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.443
- What?

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.790
- And so at the end of the night,

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.623
I just go,

00:01:03.623 --> 00:01:06.330
and it was just like probably
two, three in the morning.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.510
I go, "Prince, if you're there,

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.160
I'd love to have you
come up and sing a song."

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.470
And all of a sudden, the crowd parted,

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.510
and this purple smoke, I swear,

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.900
it's like true.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.950
It's almost like his legs
were not touching the ground.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.700
His legs were just kind of floating.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.560
And he was floating across the room,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.340
(Kelly clapping)
and I go, oh my goodness.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.040
And he comes up, and he
peels off these gloves,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.290
and he hands me his gloves.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.700
And I hand him a guitar.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.610
And not only does he play,
he plays, "Let's Go Crazy".

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:35.830
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.190
I really wish in that moment

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:38.940
you would have like, right
when he entered the stage,

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:39.773
peeled off the gloves,

00:01:39.773 --> 00:01:40.717
you would have just looked and been like,

00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:42.998
"A bit dramatic, but okay." (laughs)

00:01:42.998 --> 00:01:45.350
(audience and Jimmy laughing)

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.560
'Cause that would've
been everything. (laughs)

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.640
- I guess we're gonna do this.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.100
We rocked the house, it crushed!

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.640
It was epic!
- That's so cool, too.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.790
And, I don't know, I've
sang a bunch on "SNL",

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.996
but I've never like hosted it.

00:01:58.996 --> 00:02:00.544
And I don't know if I will now,

00:02:00.544 --> 00:02:03.120
'cause I was in New York
when Blake Shelton hosted it,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.730
and it's so much time that
y'all all spend together.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.060
I mean, y'all are like
family, (claps) like nonstop.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.760
So I can imagine at that kinda party

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.460
where you've got everybody there

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.470
and you're celebrating
all these friendships

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.210
that are like deep friendships,

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.870
y'all are around each other all the time.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.810
- You live with each other,

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:19.900
basically, at "Saturday Night Live".

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.650
I mean, we were kind of,
it's like a dorm room.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.900
It's like Horatio Sanz
and I were office mates,

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.440
and we had blankets there,

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.070
we would stay up all
night trying to write.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:31.877
And I remember Dan Aykroyd
coming in just to say,

00:02:31.877 --> 00:02:32.930
"Hi, you're the new guys.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:33.900
Just wanna say hello to you guys."

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.490
And we're like, freaking out.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.750
It was Dan Aykroyd, like, "Oh my gosh."

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.770
He's like, "Do you want me to show you

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.140
where me and John used to go?"

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.597
And I go, "Okay."

00:02:40.597 --> 00:02:41.780
And he goes, "You know,

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.260
we had all the keys to
all these rooms in 'SNL',"

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.870
and he brought me and Horatio
into someone's office,

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.790
snuck through their window, and
we're out on the 11th floor.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.700
And there's like grass up
there, and like a coy pond.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.070
It's the weirdest spot.
- What?

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.220
- And him and John used
to go up there, and right.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.710
- Yeah, they're doing
(audience and Jimmy laughing)

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:01.940
what do they call it?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.540
What did we call that on tour?

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.640
A safety meeting.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.687
That's what everybody would say,

00:03:05.687 --> 00:03:07.260
"Oh, they're at a safety meeting."

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.910
I was like, "Okay."

